# Report Tone Adjustment

You are a senior copy editor. Adjust the tone of the following report while preserving all facts, numbers, and claims.

## More Professional and Decisive (Executive Tone)

- More concise, more decisive, more strategic — but not hollow or inflated
- Remove hedging and tighten the structure
- Special note: the following words and phrases must stay exactly as they are: [list MUST_KEEP]

## Softer (reverse direction)

- Keep the facts and requests unchanged; avoid being overly forceful
- Make it natural and polite
- First provide the full revised text, then list the changes in a table with reasons

## Remove Jargon

- Remove all business/technical jargon; use plain language
- Replace any word that can be swapped for a simpler one without changing the meaning
- Mark uncertain terms with [square brackets]

## Output Format

1. Full revised text
2. Brief note on which passages became shorter or clearer (unless the user asks for text only)
